  "tool": "scripts/score_trigger_coverage.py",
  "what_this_is": "Separation for every description as it stands BEFORE the v1.18.0 rewrite. Separation = mean word-overlap coverage on the suite's positive prompts minus the mean on its negatives -- how much better this description matches the prompts that should fire it than the prompts a neighbouring skill should answer. Higher is better; the negative mean on its own is better lower.",
  "how_to_reproduce": "python3 scripts/score_trigger_coverage.py --old <ref>:<SKILL.md> --new <SKILL.md> --eval scripts/eval/<skill>.eval-suite.json --json",
  "acceptance_for_the_rewrite": "rich class must retain >=80% of its baseline separation; short class >=60%; in both classes the mean coverage on the negative prompts must not rise. Boundary clauses are exempt -- a bag of words reads a boundary as evidence for the wrong skill and a real model reads it the opposite way.",
  "caveat": "Word overlap is structurally blind to trigger-condition NARROWING: rewriting 'trigger on X -- separately watch for Y' into 'trigger on X WHOSE Y' keeps the identical word set and scores identically while the trigger now fires for fewer users. check_skill_descriptions.py --compare is the check for that class. Do not clear one with the other's number.",
